        Rule(head: Head(id: "review.selection", intent: "Before any paid work starts, each line shows how it was read and which meanings become cards; no choice is ever tentative, so none can be lost"),
            scope: Screens(["review"]),
            expectations: [
                "Rows preserve the original expression and show each sense's optional learning-language translation; different senses may resolve to different card terms",
                "Candidate rows read index Aside, term Subject, separator Aside and gloss Detail; excluded rows keep a struck term and explanation",
                "Several sense lists may stay open; a chosen sense uses a check and Detail, an unchosen sense uses Aside, and + add more remains an action in Detail",
                "An open multi-sense head reads multiple meanings: with its X/Y counter; a single-sense open head carries no repeated gloss",
                "Space commits the focused sense immediately and cannot deselect a word's last selected sense; Escape or Left collapses without discarding selections and generation needs no additional commit",
                "Down enters a head's open list and leaves + add more for the next word; C opens only eligible multi-sense rows",
                "Drop acts only from a head; dropping the last candidate returns to preserved words rather than clearing the input",
                "At most 80 selected cards may begin a fresh plan; above that [Ctrl+G] generate leaves the footer, and pressing Ctrl+G shows over the 80-card limit — deselect senses until the next walk or toggle clears the notice",
                "A successful + add more replaces the word's selection with the first new sense and focuses it; senses beyond the six-sense limit are dropped and an empty answer leaves a notice",
                "Review candidate rows are not clickable; generation guidance and alternate languages are the review's click targets",
