                "The live status shows ready against total once, then pending count when nonzero, cost and elapsed",
                "It does not repeat the exclusive unfinished remainder as a running count or claim concurrency in the sequential engine",
                "One vocabulary describes the same state in header, hints, status and glyphs",
            ],
            grounds: Grounds(
                rationale: [],
                sources: [
                    Source(file: "src/session/draft.rs", symbol: "CardPhase"),
                    Source(file: "src/tui/app.rs", symbol: "card_census"),
                    Source(file: "src/tui/screens/your_cards.rs", symbol: "status"),
                ],
                tests: [
                    Check(file: "src/session/draft.rs", test: "a_staged_rewrite_outranks_the_finished_artifacts_behind_it"),
                    Check(file: "src/session/draft.rs", test: "a_card_holding_every_artifact_is_finished"),
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "the_footer_states_the_progress_of_a_live_batch_only_as_the_ready_count"),
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "closed_pending_card_shows_the_staged_tags_and_bulk_regeneration_footer"),
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "your_cards_footer_shows_total_cost_before_every_card_finishes"),
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "failure_footer_omits_the_duplicate_terminal_count"),
                ],
            ),
        ),
        Rule(head: Head(id: "cards.viewport-follow", intent: "While a batch builds, the running card stays in view with the queued words below it, and the view never fights a learner who scrolls or opens a card"),
            scope: States([
                "cards.generating",
                "cards.retrying",
                "cards.rewriting",
                "cards.stopping",
                "cards.open",
                "cards.parked",
                "cards.scroll-end",
                "cards.published",
                "cards.partial",
            ]),
            expectations: [
                "New and restarted generation arm following and the engine selects the running card",
                "Follow aims 30 percent down the viewport, showing the unreached tail; a tall card falls back to the bottom position needed to fit its rows",
                "Reserve the completed head, three step rows and trailing blank while a followed card fills in to prevent incremental scroll creep",
                "Content bounds may lower the anchor at the batch tail; ordinary clamp and snap never cancel following",
                "Manual scroll or an arrow walk ends following; an expanded focused card, including a parked one the ride lands on, only suspends it, and collapsing that card resumes the ride",
                "On natural completion with the focused card collapsed and an outcome strip up, park once at the content end and disarm following so the strip does not slide over the card the run just finished",
                "Hold each artifact row for at least STEP_DWELL, 75 ms or three 25 ms polls, before consuming even a cached result",
            ],
            grounds: Grounds(
                rationale: [
                    "A cached step answers in a millisecond, so without the dwell a whole card would walk meta → sound → scene → picture between two frames; the dwell lives on Shell alone so console::produce and the background worker keep full speed",
                    "Parking once rather than every frame keeps the correction from fighting a later click or an opened card",
                ],
                sources: [
                    Source(file: "src/tui/app.rs", symbol: "follow_anchor"),
                    Source(file: "src/tui/app.rs", symbol: "ride_settled"),
                    Source(file: "src/tui/screens/your_cards.rs", symbol: "focused_card_range"),
                    Source(file: "src/cli/shell.rs", symbol: "poll_artifact"),
                ],
                tests: [
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "following_moves_the_selection_onto_the_card_the_engine_started"),
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "following_holds_the_running_card_a_third_of_the_way_down"),
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "following_holds_the_scroll_the_running_card_will_grow_into"),
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "scrolling_away_stops_the_viewport_following_the_engine"),
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "a_settled_batch_keeps_its_last_card_out_from_under_the_outcome_strip"),
                    Check(file: "src/cli/shell.rs", test: "a_step_holds_its_row_for_its_own_beat_before_it_settles"),
                ],
            ),
        ),
        Rule(head: Head(id: "result.outcome", intent: "A settled batch hands back folder, deck and PDF in one strip and states the number of unfinished cards exactly once, even when nothing could be saved"),
            scope: States([
                "cards.published",
                "cards.partial",
                "cards.all-failed",
                "cards.new-batch-armed",
                "cards.reopened",
                "done.published",
                "done.new-batch-armed",
            ]),
            expectations: [
                "A settled outcome strip shows FOLDER, APKG and PDF as Subject underlined labels over Detail paths behind a gutter",
                "A bold bright unfinished tag sits at the right edge level with the first output row; it is the only place the loss count is stated",
                "The loss count derives from durable published totals when present and the live census otherwise; the tag, the tagline and the Done Ctrl+G hint all ask banner::losses so they cannot disagree",
                "The strip remains visible when every card failed even if no output exists",
                "One blank row and a full-terminal dashed rule end the strip directly above the cards; rule ink and phase match the footer rule",
                "Banner height drives viewport, scroll and hit testing; publication automatically follows a drained queue with no pending rewrite",
                "A live successful batch stays on YourCards; reopening it uses Done",
                "The strip opens with the ↓ glyph and the loss tag lines up with the header's language chip at the right edge",
            ],
            grounds: Grounds(
                rationale: [
                    "How many cards never finished is said in exactly one place, so the footer, the title and the card rows never repeat or contradict it",
                ],
                sources: [
                    Source(file: "src/tui/screens/banner.rs", symbol: "losses"),
                    Source(file: "src/tui/screens/banner.rs", symbol: "height"),
                    Source(file: "src/tui/screens/banner.rs", symbol: "rule_row"),
                    Source(file: "src/tui/screens/common.rs", symbol: "render_screen"),
                ],
                tests: [
                    Check(file: "tests/snapshot.rs", test: "partial_publish_snapshot_locks_the_outcome_strip"),
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "partial_publish_is_a_settled_view_with_outputs_and_durable_tally"),
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "a_batch_that_published_nothing_still_states_what_it_lost"),
                    Check(file: "tests/snapshot.rs", test: "the_outcome_strip_closes_itself_with_the_same_rule_the_footer_uses"),
                    Check(file: "tests/your_cards.rs", test: "partial_publish_reserves_and_links_the_same_banner_rows"),
                    Check(file: "src/cli/shell.rs", test: "shell_generation_publishes_done_artifacts"),
                ],
                gaps: [
                    Gap(
                        summary: "Link and tune hit testing ignores a losses-only strip: links.rs banner_visible requires output files while the renderer also draws a strip that holds only losses, so after every card fails clicks land three rows off",
                        sources: [
                            Source(file: "src/tui/links.rs", symbol: "banner_visible"),
                            Source(file: "src/tui/screens/common.rs", symbol: "banner_visible"),
                        ],
